"Phillip Destin" <destin@emeraldcoast.com> wrote:
> Hi:
> I installed OpenVMS 7.0 on an Alpha workstation

Why didn't you install V7.1?  V7.0 was mainly intended for developers
to start developing code that took advantage of the new 64 bit stuff and
other new features.  There's no real reason to use it now that 7.1 is
out.  There should be almost no instances of third party stuff that
runs on 7.0 and not 7.1 (such as there is with 5.5-2, 6.2 etc.)

> (Alpine 275XS). After I issue the boot
> command at the console prompt, the system boots,
> but the console never gives me an X window
> (I installed DECWindows Motif 1.2-3).  Also,
> "Alpha Console" message is still displayed
> at the bottom of the screen, and the keyboard
> is disabled even as a text terminal.

I vaguely remember one of the 10000 day problems disabling DECwindows on
V7.0.  Install the appropiate patch (if not V7.1 itself).

-Mike



